# mkdir — deps.list
#
# Wave: R50 coreutil
# Doc:  design/tooling/plan.md §7 (paideia-os) for the shared-library
#       roster; design/tooling/r49-r50-plan.md §5.9 for the mkdir-specific
#       dependency set.
#
# One row per shared-library dependency. Each row is a semver pin against
# the library's dual-signed 1.0 release. `pkg install mkdir` resolves
# this list transitively at install time and refuses the install if any
# row's dual-sig verification fails.
#
# Row format (I3-consistent with libpdx-argv, libpdx-cap):
#   <name>@<semver> <ml-dsa-65-author-fp> <ml-dsa-65-paideia-root-fp>
#
# The two fingerprints let `pkg verify` short-circuit re-verification
# when the local pkg store already holds the matching signed manifest.
# Fingerprint format: 16 hex chars = truncated BLAKE3-256 of the
# ML-DSA-65 public key (matches libpdx-cap M3-001 KIND_USER_ref fp).
#
# Placeholder-until-signing-bot: every `PLACEHOLDER_*_FP` entry is
# replaced with the real fingerprint at the M5-002 mirror-push step
# once the paideia-signing-bot host is stood up (T-INFRA-002 in
# design/tooling/plan.md §10). The row structure is frozen at v1.0;
# only the fingerprint hex changes.

# --- mkdir.ENH-009 correction (post-1.0.0, milestone #6) ---
#
# This file previously pinned libpdx-cap, libpdx-audit, and
# libpdx-semantic-pipe alongside libpdx-argv, on the assumption that
# mkdir linked all four. A grep-verified audit of src/ (see
# design/enhancement-plan.md §3.7 and the mkdir.ENH-008 investigation)
# found exactly one cross-module symbol actually called from _start's
# reachable graph: `reset` + `parse_argv`, both libpdx-argv. Per this
# file's own header, `pkg install mkdir` resolves every pinned row
# transitively and REFUSES the install if that row's dual-sig
# verification fails — so the three dropped rows below were pure
# supply-chain surface for zero linked benefit; a tool should not make
# its own installability depend on a library it does not call.
#
# `manifest.pdxsig [deps]` still lists all four rows as of this
# correction — that section is part of the signed manifest body,
# frozen at v1.0 per design/tooling/plan.md §D4 ("the signing bot MUST
# NOT rewrite §1 during re-sign or the hash chain breaks"), so
# reconciling it is deferred to the next signed manifest revision
# rather than hand-edited here. This file (deps.list) is not part of
# that signed body and is safe to correct immediately.

# --- Real dependency set (grep-verified) ---

libpdx-argv@1.0.0                  PLACEHOLDER_LPDX_ARGV_AUTHOR_FP  PLACEHOLDER_PAIDEIA_ROOT_FP

# --- v1.0 does NOT depend on: ---
#
# libpdx-cap — mkdir declares five caps in caps.decl / _init_caps, but
#   `cap_manifest_verify` is never called (mkdir.ENH-008 confirmed this
#   is zero call sites repo-wide AND ecosystem-wide: even the shell's
#   own exec path does its own inline cap narrowing rather than calling
#   into libpdx-cap for it). Cap-delivery enforcement for mkdir is the
#   kernel loader's InitCap validator, not a libpdx-cap userspace call.
#   Re-add this pin only if/when mkdir grows a real libpdx-cap call
#   site (e.g. a future self-check variant of cap_manifest_verify).
#
# libpdx-audit — `emit_audit_event` (src/mkdir.pdx) is a hand-rolled
#   raw `sys_cap_invoke` against the KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT at SLOT_AUDIT_EP,
#   not a libpdx-audit library call. Re-add this pin if/when
#   emit_audit_event is rewritten to route through a real libpdx-audit
#   marshalling call (its own doc comment already flags this as a
#   likely M3-substrate-002 follow-up).
#
# libpdx-semantic-pipe — `send_record` is never called and cap slot 3
#   (the semantic pipe) is never invoked; `caps.decl` and
#   `manifest.pdxsig` both declare `CreatedDirRecord@0.1` as an output
#   schema, but nothing in src/ marshals a record through this library.
#   Tracked as mkdir.ENH-002 (`--json` + live slot-3 emit, milestone #6,
#   open); re-add this pin when that lands with a real `send_record`
#   call site.
#
# libpdx-elevate — mkdir writes only inside the invoker's subtree; the
#   cross-user / cross-subtree elevate hop is out of scope for v1.0 per
#   design/tooling/r49-r50-plan.md §5.9. Adding it is a post-1.0 minor
#   bump.
#
# pdx-regex, pdx-time, pdx-help, pdx-color — no pattern, no time input,
#   no color output at v1.0. --help lives in doc/mkdir.pdxdoc and is
#   rendered by the `doc` tool at read time.
#
# pdx-tls, libpaideia-ui — no network reach, no GUI variant.

# EOF
